{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000 at ~48.5% acc), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality carries meaningful signal for this task. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest test of this question: it matches config_001 on profile setting (singleprofile) and uses a standard, well-calibrated image encoder, so the primary variable is modality itself. If image-only substantially outperforms RNA-only, the search should pivot toward image encoders and multimodal fusion; if it performs similarly or worse, RNA remains the primary signal and we should explore RNA encoders and multiprofile aggregation. Resolving this structural question first maximizes information gain per experiment and prevents wasting budget on secondary design choices (aggregation, fusion strategy, encoder variants) before knowing which modality is most informative."
}

